# Narrowly scoped on purpose: this repository has no line-ending policy of its
# own, and imposing one here would renormalise thousands of files.
#
# These two are checked out with LF regardless of core.autocrlf because the
# Docker build is the only consumer that reads them and it reads them as a
# shell script would. On a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true they would
# otherwise arrive with CRLF, and every backslash line-continuation in the
# Dockerfile would carry a trailing carriage return into the RUN command.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf

# A shebang only works if the file is checked out with LF, and this repo has
# core.autocrlf users; without this the script fails to run on their machines.
sql/touch_migration.sh text eol=lf
